## 15. Phased Implementation Plan

### Phase 0 — Foundation and safety

**Scope:** Baseline testing, module extraction, auth/SSRF hardening, environment validation, database and queue setup.

**Deliverables:** Stable legacy baseline, feature flags, migrations, worker framework.

**Exit criteria:** Existing core flows pass; new features disabled by default.

### Phase 1 — RSS News Radar

**Scope:** Feed manager, parser, scheduler, canonical URL processing, deduplication and ranking.

**Deliverables:** Working news dashboard and durable story clusters.

**Exit criteria:** Multiple feeds can be polled repeatedly without duplicated stories.

### Phase 2 — Editorial Intelligence

**Scope:** Evidence collection, claim verification, structured scripts, manual editing, real speech timing.

**Deliverables:** Evidence-backed editable episode with accurate audio manifest.

**Exit criteria:** Unsupported material claims are flagged and captions align to actual narration timing.

### Phase 3 — Video Director and Renderer

**Scope:** Deterministic scene manifest, reusable studio components, Remotion composition, MP4 rendering, quality validation.

**Deliverables:** First real three-minute Pixel Marcus video.

**Exit criteria:** `VID-01` through `VID-10` pass.

### Phase 4 — Review and YouTube

**Scope:** Review UI, revision approvals, OAuth, private upload, scheduling, audit trail.

**Deliverables:** Supervised publishing.

**Exit criteria:** All review and YouTube acceptance tests pass, including denial of unapproved publication.

### Phase 5 — Production hardening

**Scope:** Monitoring, retries, cost controls, failure recovery, license verification, media rights, operational dashboards.

**Deliverables:** Production-ready daily video workflow.

**Exit criteria:** Five consecutive end-to-end episode productions complete with no critical failures; at least one uses the actual approved YouTube publishing path.

